<main id="main" class="container account-page">
    <div class="account-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR PRACTICE. YOUR PRIVACY.</p><h1>NISHA mobile privacy.</h1><p class="muted">These details describe the Android and iOS app provided by NISHA at nishaglobal.com.</p></div></div>
    <section class="dashboard-panel"><h2>Information used by the app</h2><p>Creating an account sends your name, email and chosen password to NISHA over HTTPS. Passwords are stored as hashes. Signed-in access tokens are kept in Android Keystore-backed storage or iOS Keychain. The browser preview keeps its token in memory only.</p><p>Online practice answers, saved results, requested AI feedback and account access records are stored by the NISHA website. Local offline results, preferences and unfinished practice stay on the device. They can be cleared in the app's account controls. Offline results are not silently uploaded as verified exam results.</p><p>Login and account-security controls use limited request metadata and hashed rate-limit keys to reduce misuse. The app does not include advertising SDKs, contact access, location collection or third-party analytics SDKs.</p></section>
    <section class="dashboard-panel"><h2>Microphone and AI feedback</h2><p>Microphone permission is requested when you choose to record. Recordings are temporary and are not automatically uploaded. Leaving the recording flow or clearing the recording discards it. Listening uses the phone's speech service; voice availability depends on the device.</p><p>If you request an AI review, the selected response and relevant task context are sent through NISHA to OpenAI. Selecting a recording also sends that recording for transcription. Feedback is saved to your account when available. Reviews have request limits and are practice guidance, not official IELTS or PTE scores. Speaking feedback based on a transcript cannot assess pronunciation or delivery.</p></section>
    <section class="dashboard-panel"><h2>Coaching and purchases</h2><p>Approved coaching videos load from the owner's configured video host. Limited watch-progress records can support teacher rewards. Video playback needs a connection. Store purchase support must be configured before in-app purchases are offered; this testing build does not collect card details.</p></section>
    <section class="dashboard-panel"><h2>Delete your account or device data</h2><p>In the app, open Account, choose the deletion request action and confirm your current password. You can also submit the request on this website. A request signs you out across devices and enters the owner's deletion queue. It is a receipt, not a claim that removal has already completed.</p><p>The owner should process requests within 30 days. Personal account and practice data are removed or anonymised during completion. Records needed for payment, accounting, disputes, fraud prevention or legal obligations may be retained for the applicable legal period, with access restricted to the business. Removing the app alone does not delete your website account.</p><a class="btn btn-outline" href="delete-account.php">Request account deletion →</a><p>Use the student support contact shown in the footer for privacy questions or help accessing an account. The owner must configure that contact and publish any additional business-specific retention information before store release.</p></section>
